{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01U43nk2o9n36kHvfcNuMhTX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator), not ship utilities.\n\n**Architecture**: Specifications (docs/specs/) drive code generation into cmd/ (one package per utility) and pkg/ (shared libraries: sys, format, testutils, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil). Differential testing via pkg/testutils compares Go binaries against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Implementation state**: Many releases are code-complete (rel00.0 partial, rel01.2-03.0 done, rel02.0-02.2 done). The current frontier is **rel04.0 (ls)**, which is partially implemented — R1.x through R3.3 are complete per recent commits (tasks 5215, 5217). Requirements R3.4 through R4.9 remain \"ready\" (21 requirements).\n\n**Current release**: rel04.0 (ls). R3.4-R4.9 are ready. All earlier releases with requirement_states entries are complete.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nEarliest incomplete release with ready requirements: **rel04.0** (ls, srd008-ls). Requirements R3.4-R4.9 are all status \"ready\". The package already exists with partial implementation, so no contract task is needed. All dependencies (pkg/sys, pkg/format) are in place since earlier ls requirements already compiled.\n\nNext after rel04.0: rel04.1 (realpath, readlink, pwd, tty, logname) — all requirements ready but these are new packages needing contracts.\n\nWith 4 task limit, I'll continue ls implementation: 4 batches of 4 requirements each (R3.4-R4.4), leaving R4.5-R4.9 for a future batch.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight=1 (no weight overrides available in context):\n\n- Task 0: R3.4 (w=1) + R3.5 (w=1) + R3.6 (w=1) + R3.7 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: R3.8 (w=1) + R3.9 (w=1) + R3.10 (w=1) + R3.11 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: R3.12 (w=1) + R3.13 (w=1) + R3.14 (w=1) + R3.15 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: R4.1 (w=1) + R4.2 (w=1) + R4.3 (w=1) + R4.4 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ls: features implementation (srd008-ls R3.4-R3.7)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml (requirements R3.4, R3.5, R3.6, R3.7)\n      - cmd/ls/main.go (existing ls implementation -- extend, do not rewrite)\n      - cmd/ls/ls_test.go (existing differential tests -- add new test cases)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (FileInfo struct used for file metadata)\n      - pkg/format/humansize.go (HumanSize formatting used by ls)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (color output support)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd008-ls R3.4-R3.7\n      - path: cmd/ls/ls_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases exercising R3.4-R3.7\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls requirement R3.4 -- read the SRD for the full specification of this requirement and implement all acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls requirement R3.5 -- read the SRD for the full specification of this requirement and implement all acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls requirement R3.6 -- read the SRD for the full specification of this requirement and implement all acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd008-ls requirement R3.7 -- read the SRD for the full specification of this requirement and implement all acceptance criteria\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing cmd/ls/main.go implementation. Do not restructure or rewrite existing code -- add the new features incrementally on top of what is already there.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/sys.Stat and pkg/sys.Lstat for file metadata. Use pkg/format for output formatting, color, and column alignment. Do not duplicate syscall or formatting logic in cmd/ls/.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Add differential test cases using the existing testutils.RunDiffTests pattern. The reference binary is gls (exec.LookPath). Skip if reference binary is not found. Set LC_ALL=C in test environment.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main if not already present.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"srd008-ls requirements R3.4, R3.5, R3.6, and R3.7 are fully implemented per their SRD acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Differential test cases added for each new feature, covering the flag/behavior specified in each requirement\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/ls/ succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/ls/... -count=1 passes (tests skip gracefully if gls reference binary is not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/ls/ reports no issues\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ls: features implementation (srd008-ls R3.8-R3.11)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml (requirements R3.8, R3.9, R3.10, R3.11)\n      - cmd/ls/main.go (existing ls implementation -- extend, do not rewrite)\n      - cmd/ls/ls_test.go (existing differential tests -- add new test cases)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (FileInfo struct used for file metadata)\n      - pkg/format/humansize.go (HumanSize formatting used by ls)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (color output support)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd008-ls R3.8-R3.11\n      - path: cmd/ls/ls_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add dif